==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|упасть|alt1=упад-|-ок}}. Probably adapted as an [[enlightenment]] term mid-18th century after {{clq|ru|pl|upadek|notext=1}}, also {{m|pl|upad}}, both also in the most literal senses of falling (on the head), the setting of the Sun etc., for the Latinate terms of {{m|en|decadence}}, a recurring idea in such works as Montesquieu’s {{w|Considerations on the Causes of the Greatness of the Romans and their Decline}} and Edward Gibbon’s {{w|History of the Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire}}, and their Russian titles.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|упа́док}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Rominf-упадок.wav}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|упа́док|*}}

# [[decline]], [[decay]], [[decadence]]
#: {{syn|ru|увяда́ние}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[приходи́ть]] [[в]] '''упа́док'''|to decay}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[в]] [[состояние|состоя́нии]] '''упа́дка'''|in decline}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[до]] [[состояние|состоя́ния]] '''упа́дка'''|to a state of decline}}
# [[collapse]], [[breakdown]], [[decline]]
#: {{ant|ru|расцве́т}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''упа́док''' [[дух|ду́ха]]|despondency; low spirits; depression}}

